--TEST--
A bare name in value position is `E0319` and a bare call is `E0320`, never a panic — ADR 0011 §§ 1 and 3 removed the global-function and global-constant storage rows outright, so neither name resolves against anything
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:statements/storage-that-outlives-a-call`: a constant always belongs to a class, so a bare name in
// value position has nothing to resolve against.
echo PHP_EOL;
// `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`: the same for a free function. The callee is the identical
// AST node as the line above, and it is reported as a *function* rather
// than as a constant because only one of the two replacements is right.
echo strlen("abc");
// The control, and the whole reason a class side is skipped rather than
// walked: the same name-shaped node on the left of a `::` means a class,
// so neither refusal fires here and the expectation below carries no
// diagnostic for either line.
final class Limit {
    public const int MAX = 9;
}
echo Limit::MAX;
echo Core\Str::length("abc");
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0319]: `PHP_EOL` is not a constant that exists
  --> %s:4:6
  |
4 | echo PHP_EOL;
  |      ^^^^^^^ no global constant has this name
  = help: `rule:statements/storage-that-outlives-a-call`: a constant always belongs to a class, so there is no global one to fetch — write `Class::NAME`, and a built-in constant is on its `Core` class, such as `Core\Math::PI`

error[E0320]: `strlen` is not a function that exists
  --> %s:8:6
  |
8 | echo strlen("abc");
  |      ^^^^^^ no free function has this name
  = help: `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`: every callable is a method, and the built-ins live under the reserved `Core` namespace — `Core\Str::length($s)`, or `use Core\Str;` and then `Str::length($s)`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
